  "snippet": "#​644 — October 15, 2026 Read on the Web 📝 We're taking next week off and will be back on Thursday, October 29.__Peter Cooper, your editor Skia Canvas 4.0: A Fast Canvas Environment for Node — Based on Google's Skia grap...",
  "coverImage": "https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/v1653576619/lgfqinzbdqttwmhvljxb.png",
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​644 — October 15, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191618/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>📝 We're taking next week off and will be back on Thursday, October 29.<br/>__<br/>Peter Cooper, your editor</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; margin: 0; padding: 0;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/v1653576619/lgfqinzbdqttwmhvljxb.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"100%\"/></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191575/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/hjm5qc2crdbtnm3m0qft.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191575/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"skia-canvas.org\">Skia Canvas 4.0: A Fast Canvas Environment for Node</a></span> — Based on Google's Skia graphics engine, it produces results similar to Chrome's own canvas. GPU accelerated and can render images, paths, fonts, shapes, etc. both to static images <em>and</em> live in a native window. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191576/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">v4.0</a> is faster, lighter, and adds native PDF loading. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191577/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub repo.</a></p>\n<p>Christian Swinehart </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191574/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"110\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/b4ec5cf1.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"110\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191574/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.warpbuild.com\">Cut Your GitHub Actions Times and Costs in Half</a></span> — Faster Node builds with better hardware, unlimited concurrency, no queueing delays, and no commitments. Change one line and get started with $50 in free credits using code <code>START50</code>.</p>\n<p>WarpBuild <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\">▶  <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191578/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.youtube.com\">The NodeConf EU 2026 Talks</a></span> — <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191579/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">NodeConf EU</a> took place in Italy a few weeks ago and the talks just dropped onto YouTube today, covering topics from Node's <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191580/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">new FFI features</a> and <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191581/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">Emscripten and WebAssembly</a> to <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191582/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">V8 heap management</a> and <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191583/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">performance profiling</a>.</p>\n<p>NodeConf EU / YouTube </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191584/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Deno is joining Cloudflare</a> to work on folding <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191585/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">celld</a> into <code>workerd</code>. Deno itself will get a year of updates before, hopefully, becoming community-maintained.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191586/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Node.js v26.12.0 (Current)</a> has been released. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191587/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Configuration files</a> are now stable as a way to define runtime, test, watch and permission settings.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191588/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Node.js v24.22.0 (LTS)</a> has also been released and brings <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191589/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\"><code>util.throttle</code></a> and <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191590/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\"><code>util.debounce</code></a> to the LTS release.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🔒 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191591/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Security releases of Node are expected next Wednesday, October 21</a> across 26.x, 24.x and 22.x release lines to fix at least one 'HIGH' severity issue. Also, Node 24 enters maintenance on October 20, and Node 26 becomes the active LTS line on October 28, the day Node 27's first alpha is expected.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191592/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"aws.amazon.com\">Using <em>AWS Lambda Web Functions</em> for Deploying Node Apps</a></span> — Amazon has launched <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191593/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">AWS Lambda Web Functions</a>, a way to run <em>standard</em> HTTP apps (using Express, Hono, Fastify, etc.) on Lambda without needing to rewrite your code around an event handler.</p>\n<p>Wood, Wendt, and Karak (Amazon) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><span>📊</span> <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191594/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"lemire.me\">WebSocket Servers in JavaScript: Node.js vs Bun vs Deno</a></span> — It's great to see a win for Node 26 with uWebSockets.js here, with its results getting close to C's low levels of latency, ahead of Bun and Deno.</p>\n<p>Daniel Lemire </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191595/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"clickhouse.com\">Up to 10x Faster Postgres for I/O-Heavy Workloads</a></span> — Managed Postgres on local NVMe, natively integrated with ClickHouse for real-time analytics.</p>\n<p>ClickHouse Managed Postgres <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191596/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Zod 4 Got Rid of a Bunch of CPUs for Us</a> – Up to 31% less CPU after upgrading from Zod 3. <cite>Chris Arderne (Trigger.dev)</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191597/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Fast Node.js is Mostly About Doing Less</a> <cite>Ishtmeet Singh (NodeBook)</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191598/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">The Disappointing Death of Deno</a> <cite>Brett Chalupa</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>🛠 Code &amp; Tools</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191599/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"tanstack.com\">TanStack Start 1.0: A Full-Stack Framework Reaches Stability</a></span> — The increasingly popular full-stack framework for React and Solid goes stable, bringing typed server functions and streaming SSR to apps deployed on Node, Bun, Cloudflare Workers and other targets. Here's <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191600/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\">how it compares to Next.js</a>.</p>\n<p>Tanner Linsley et al. </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191601/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"imapkit.com\">ImapKit: A Scriptable IMAP Server for Testing Email Clients</a></span> — An embeddable IMAP server for testing mail clients, with in-memory mailboxes, extensions for numerous IMAP features, and scripted 'faults' to test robustness. Runs inside your tests or can be driven from other languages via a REST API.</p>\n<p>Postal Systems OÜ </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><span>⭐</span> <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191604/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">Express 5.3 Released</a></span> — No big new features, but a large number of bug fixes and minor improvements, including to security.</p>\n<p>Express.js Team </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 500 !important; font-size: 18px !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191605/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.bram.us\">caniname: CLI Tool to Check Project Name Availability on Netlify and npm</a></span> — It's also easy to add checks for other systems.</p>\n<p>Bramus van Damme </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191606/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">fast-cli 6.0</a> – Sindre Sorhus's tool to run download/upload speed tests. A neat way to quickly test speeds as you can run it with <code>npx -y fast-cli</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191607/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">p-queue 10.0</a> – Promise queue with concurrency control and rate limiting. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191608/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">v10 has zero dependencies</a>, becomes an <code>EventTarget</code>, and runs tasks in the caller's <code>AsyncLocalStorage</code> context.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191609/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\"><code>actions/setup-node</code> 7.1</a> – GitHub's official Action for installing Node in CI workflows. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191610/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">It can now read the Node version</a> from a <code>mise.toml</code> file.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191611/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Happy DOM 21.0</a> – JavaScript implementation of a browser without a GUI, popular for testing. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191612/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">v21 disables external stylesheet and <code>iframe</code> loading by default</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191613/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">p-map 7.1</a> – Library to map over promises concurrently. <a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191614/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Now with <code>pMapSettled</code></a>, keyed variants for objects and <code>Map</code>s, and <code>pMapStop</code> to break out early.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191615/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">RandExp.js 0.6</a> – Library to generate random strings that match a regex.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191616/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824B; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">node-oracledb 26.0</a> – Oracle's official <em>Oracle Database</em> driver.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<div style=\"margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"></div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 0.8em; font-weight: bold; color: #009900;\">Overheard on Hacker News</span></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 20px;\">\n<p>“Why reimplement Node? It works. Marginal performance or UX or security benefits are not enough.”</p>\n<p>___<br/><a href=\"https://nodeweekly.com/link/191617/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #20824b !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Ryan Dahl</a> on the news that Deno is joining Cloudflare.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
  "attachments": []
}